  71:../../opus/celt/entenc.c **** /*Outputs a symbol, with a carry bit.
  72:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****   If there is a potential to propagate a carry over several symbols, they are
  73:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****    buffered until it can be determined whether or not an actual carry will
  74:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****    occur.
  75:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****   If the counter for the buffered symbols overflows, then the stream becomes
  76:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****    undecodable.
  77:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****   This gives a theoretical limit of a few billion symbols in a single packet on
  78:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****    32-bit systems.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\oleg\AppData\Local\Temp\cc9jKrCk.s 			page 5


  79:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****   The alternative is to truncate the range in order to force a carry, but
  80:../../opus/celt/entenc.c ****    requires similar carry tracking in the decoder, needlessly slowing it down.*/
